  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "One molar <math> <mrow>  <mtext>(1</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>M)</mtext></mrow></math> aqueous solution is more concentrated than one molal aqueous solution of the same solute. In solution, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> provides three ions. While <math > <mrow>  <mtext>NaCl</mtext></mrow></math> provides two ions. Hence, vapour pressure of solution of <math > <mrow>  <mtext>NaCl</mtext></mrow></math> is higher (as it gives less ions). Therefore, <math > <mrow>  <mtext>1</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>molal</mtext><mtext>&#x2004;</mtext><mtext>NaCl</mtext></mrow></math> will have the maximum vapour pressure.",
